        "explanation": "This dictates how objects are cloned in memory.\n- **Shallow Copy:** Copies the top-level object, but all inner object fields are just copied as reference pointers. If the original modifies an inner object, the clone changes too.\n- **Deep Copy:** Recursively copies the top-level object AND creates brand new physical copies of all inner objects. The original and clone are 100% physically severed.",
